> Use tables if you want to avoid text appearing under the links.

Please don't use tables for layout.  That would be Bad and Wrong.  The 
use of div sections and stylesheets should be used to obtain the same 
effect, without munging things for people requiring accessible user 
agents.  Accessibility is really important IMHO.

Tables should be used for representing tabulated data, not fiddling 
layout.

As quoth the w3c:

"Tables should not be used purely as a means to layout document content 
as this may present problems when rendering to non-visual media. 
Additionally, when used with graphics, these tables may force users to 
scroll horizontally to view a table designed on a system with a larger 
display. To minimize these problems, authors should use style sheets to 
control layout rather than tables."

